	(text "BUS INTERFACE: THE SIX PORTS' STROBES, THE CHIP'S CS, RS AND R/W, ITS DATA BUFFER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "69d920a1-89da-5b4d-a61d-d2f831313be6"))
	(text "X1: the YACC1 V3.2 bus (DIN 41612). IC2 (writes) and IC3 (reads) decode IO-ADDR0-3: ports PA-PF = 1010-1111.\nCS (IC4) = any of OUT PA, OUT PB, IN PC, IN PD. RS = IO-ADDR0 and R/W = IO-ADDR2 through IC39, a latch that CS\ncloses: an IN record drops the port number with its strobe, and the chip wants them until CS has risen.\nIC5 between the chip's D0-7 and the bus: enabled by CS, direction R/W. IC30/A: -RESET to the chip's RES and DACK." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "27b3c551-e8eb-591b-8e9b-b2e882c6ebd1"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
